## 🛠️ Code Implementations

### 1. Dynamic Terminal Clock (Recursive Pattern)
This utility captures high-resolution timestamps using the native `Date` object and breaks down 24-hour intervals into symmetric 12-hour components (AM/PM layouts) with automated left-hand character padding.

```javascript
const updateClock = () => {
    const now = new Date();

    // 24-hour format
    const hours24 = now.getHours().toString().padStart(2, '0');
    const minutes = now.getMinutes().toString().padStart(2, '0');
    const seconds = now.getSeconds().toString().padStart(2, '0');
    
    // 12-hour format calculation
    const hours12 = ((now.getHours() + 11) % 12 + 1).toString().padStart(2, '0');
    const ampm = now.getHours() >= 12 ? 'PM' : 'AM';
    
    console.log(`24-hour format: ${hours24}:${minutes}:${seconds}`);
    console.log(`12-hour format: ${hours12}:${minutes}:${seconds} ${ampm}`);

    // Self-scheduling callback wrapper ensures safe execution gaps
    setTimeout(updateClock, 1000);
};

updateClock();
```

### 2. Modern Promisified Sleep Utility
A linear, sequential script showing how to wrap legacy asynchronous timing routines inside cleaner ES6 `Promise` bodies using modern `async/await` syntax structures.

```javascript
function sleep(second) {
  return new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, second * 1000));
}

async function hello() {
  console.log("Good Morning");
  await sleep(3); 
  
  console.log("Nithin");
  await sleep(2); 
  
  console.log("How was your promise journey?");
  await sleep(4); 
  
  console.log("It's completed!");
}

hello();
```

